# Theme template strings whose SOURCE text is Lithuanian — this file supplies
# the English shown on /en/ pages.
#
# Naming/locale notes (learned the hard way, do not "fix"):
#   - Theme .mo files must be named <locale>.mo (en_GB.mo), NOT
#     workernu-<locale>.mo — load_theme_textdomain() only looks for the
#     locale-only name inside the theme's /languages dir.
#   - The English locale must be en_GB, not en_US: WordPress hard-skips
#     loading any en_US translation file (it assumes source strings are
#     already English — ours are Lithuanian).
# The workernu-lang plugin maps /en/… requests to the en_GB locale.
#
# Regenerate the .mo after editing:  wp i18n make-mo <this directory>

